{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Vanavaccha (2nd)","html":"<article id='thag1.113'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.113 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.113 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dvādasamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Twelve </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Vanavacchattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Vanavaccha (2nd) </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Acchodikā puthusilā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The water’s clear and the rocks are broad, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>gonaṅgulamigāyutā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>monkeys and deer are all around; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ambusevālasañchannā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>festooned with dewy moss, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>te selā ramayanti man”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>these rocky crags delight me! </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Vanavaccho thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
